    "recurrence": "c[n] = b*d[n] + s[n-1], s[n]=b*d[n]+a*c[n], d=old-new; hence c[n]=b*d[n]+b*d[n-1]+a*c[n-1].",
    "transfer": "H(z)=b(1+z^-1)/(1-a*z^-1). 1-H=(1-b)(1-z^-1)/(1-a*z^-1) because a+ b=1-b.",
    "causality": "Current/past samples only. One zeroed scalar state per channel, retained across block boundaries.",
    "stability": "0<a<1 gives absolutely summable impulse. h[0]=b; h[n>=1]=b(1+a)*a^(n-1), positive and summing to 1. Stable BIBO bound |H*d|<=sup|d| in exact arithmetic.",
    "DC_Nyquist": "H(1)=2b/(1-a)=1, H(-1)=0. DC old, Nyquist new.",
    "unit_circle": "Writing t=tan(w/2), H=k/(k+j*t), 1-H=j*t/(k+j*t), so |H|^2+|1-H|^2=1 and H+(1-H)=1 in exact arithmetic. This does not guarantee absence of cancellation/boost between different correlated old/new streams.",
    "common_board": "If old=B+Cold,new=B+Cnew, Y=B+H*Cold+(1-H)*Cnew in exact arithmetic. Existing float reductions/output quantization can leave tiny numerical residuals; do not claim bit-exact board component preservation.",
    "mechanics": "Pure output postprocessing receives only audio; no instrument state or generalized force exists here. Source-pair mechanical trajectory/force evidence is inherited, not rerun.",
    "precision": "float64 recurrence on float32 source WAVs; one final float32 output quantization. Signed-zero conditional is mathematically zero correction and retains identical-input bit signs."
